Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 09:53:11 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] =?UTF-8?q?=EF=BB=BFci(release):=20a=20site=5Fonly=20dispa?=
 =?UTF-8?q?tch=20can=20take=20the=20app=20of=20an=20earlier=20run?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A site_only dispatch skips the wasm job, so the site goes out with app/
as its "not part of this copy" page. The new optional dispatch input
app_run_id names an earlier run (the release's tag run). With site_only,
the site job downloads that run's wasm-app artifact (run-id, job token,
actions: read) and checks it with web/check-app-page.sh. On this path a
failed download or check fails the job, so nothing deploys. The tag
path, a plain dispatch and site_only without the input are unchanged.

Refs #3276

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
